# Work Layer

This layer answers: "How does {{REPO_NAME}} hold work entrypoints and execution context?"

Work stores public-safe work indexes, project entrypoints, collaboration context, and execution surfaces. It may point to an external private wiki, project repo, runtime sessions, artifacts, or docs, but it must not copy private customer material, meeting text, commercial secrets, or unauthorized work material.

When work facts need long-term storage, route them to memory or an external authority source. When work lessons become reusable, route them to runtime lessons and evolution.
